{
  "name": "cloud_cover",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§22 partial cloud cover: the off/on true-no-op invariant (off must read exactly 0, not merely low — see CelestialLightingFeatures' own note on what a flag being off must reproduce), then an hourly drift survey under fixed Clear weather from noon to 8pm on day 40 at latitude 45 (cloud_cover_fraction only has an opinion while curWeather == Clear — see Patch_CloudCoverSky's gate). Values are exact live measurements from this fixture/tile/season, pinned live per the parent CLAUDE.md rule (never replace a measured pin with a computed one); a preset or noise-constant change invalidates the whole ladder and it must be re-run, not re-derived. The A/B screenshot pair sits at hour 16, the surveyed peak (0.2710), for the strongest visible contrast.",
